    {"q": "In what year was the empire permanently divided between Theodosius’s sons?", "options": ["AD 117", "AD 330", "AD 395", "AD 476"], "answer": 2, "explain": ["117 is roughly when the empire was at its largest.", "330 is when Constantinople was founded.", "Correct. After Theodosius I died, Arcadius ruled the East and Honorius the West, and the empire was never reunited.", "476 is when the last western emperor was deposed."]},
    {"q": "What city became the eastern capital?", "options": ["Alexandria", "Antioch", "Constantinople", "Athens"], "answer": 2, "explain": ["Alexandria was a huge, rich city, but it wasn’t the imperial capital.", "Antioch was an important eastern city, but not the capital.", "Correct. Founded by Constantine in 330, it’s modern Istanbul.", "Athens was a cultural centre, not the seat of government."]},
    {"q": "Which was a major advantage of the Eastern empire?", "options": ["It spoke Latin", "It had a richer economy and tax base", "It had no external enemies", "It was smaller than a single province"], "answer": 1, "explain": ["The East mostly spoke Greek, and the language didn’t make it stronger anyway.", "Correct. More cities and trade meant more taxes to pay soldiers and buy off invaders.", "It faced Persia and many raiders. It could just afford to deal with them.", "It was a vast empire in its own right."]},
    {"q": "How long did the Eastern (Byzantine) empire outlast the Western one?", "options": ["About 10 years", "About 100 years", "Almost 1,000 years", "It fell first"], "answer": 2, "explain": ["Far longer than that.", "Much longer still.", "Correct. It fell in 1453, nearly 1,000 years after the West’s end in 476.", "The West fell first, in 476."]}
