    {"q": "Who first formalized comparative advantage, in 1817?", "options": ["Adam Smith", "David Ricardo", "Karl Marx", "John Maynard Keynes"], "answer": 1, "explain": ["Smith wrote about the division of labour and absolute advantage in 1776.", "Correct. Ricardo used England, Portugal, cloth and wine.", "Marx came later and focused on other questions.", "Keynes worked in the 20th century, mostly on recessions."]},
    {"q": "What does comparative advantage NOT guarantee?", "options": ["That total output can rise", "That every individual worker gains", "That specialization is possible", "That trade can benefit both countries overall"], "answer": 1, "explain": ["It does show that total output can rise.", "Correct. Some workers in shrinking industries can lose, even while the country as a whole gains.", "Specialization is exactly what it recommends.", "That’s the main claim, at the national level."]}
